  "step_3": "The decision reason requires focusing on the maximum loss and treating it as more important than gains. However, in the verbal report, the individual acknowledges the outcome difference but dismisses it as unimportant, and instead bases their decision on probabilities. There is no mention of losses being weighted more heavily than gains, nor is there any indication that the worst outcome (0 Euros) was a central consideration. Moreover, since both lotteries have the same maximum loss (0 Euros), even if the individual had considered it, no preference would arise from this reason. The information considered by the individual (probabilities, near-equality of outcomes) does not align with the core of the decision reason (loss dominance, maximum loss comparison). The justification is probability-based, not loss-averse. Therefore, there is no evidence that the decision reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
